'' THE CAST-THEN-CONSTRUCTOR CHAINS fbc-modern TAKES still build, beside the ones
'' tests/diagnostics/cast-ctor-chain refuses: a numeric cast that CONVERTS into the
'' constructor's parameter (double and ulong into 'byval as long'), a string cast into a string
'' constructor, and a cast yielding EXACTLY the constructor's typed pointer ('long ptr',
'' 'zstring ptr') -- as an argument, an operand, an initialiser, 'T( x )' and a result. The
'' pointer chains were TKO0698 (refused) or dropped: StructorCastCost had no pointer arm, nor
'' lowering one (lowerctor.bas, lowercallarg.bas -- UserCastToPtr_).
''
'' A goldenrun.sh differential: built and run by fbc-modern 1.20 and by tiko, the two
'' outputs are byte-identical (measured 2026-10-10).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/driver/src/cast-ctor-chain-accepted.bas -o tests/driver/castctorchain.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/castctorchain.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/castctorchain.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: arg 3 9 41 7 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: opfalsetrue
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: init 9 41
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ctor 7 41
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ret 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
